
# An example query module. A package holds two kinds of `.tree` file: documents (which compose widgets) and query
# modules (which read the word.surf base API). A query module is a Term `task`. This one, `nouns`, returns a
# project's nouns by calling the base client's language-word filter, which a document binds a `paradigm` or `gloss`
# widget to. The base client is docked as a host module (`dock load`), so the call lowers to a base API call
# (`wordApi.filterLanguageWords({ project, role: 'noun' })`) on each backend. Wiring the docked handle to a live,
# authenticated base client is the remaining binding; the query shape and its lowering are shown here.

dock load
  load <@cluesurf/seed/word>, name word-api

# the base filter this query builds: the project scope and the grammatical role
form noun-query
  link project, like text
  link role, like text

task nouns
  take project, like text
  like dynamic
  send back
    call word-api/filter-language-words
      make noun-query
        bind project, read project
        bind role, text <noun>
